<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dead Sea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dead Sea is a salt lake in the Jordan Rift Valley between Jordan to the east and Israel and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a> to the west, its shore the lowest land on Earth. In antiquity the kingdom of Moab lay on the plateau east of it. In the crusader and Ayyubid periods the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-karak">Kerak</a>, east of the sea, controlled routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dead-sea.jpg" alt="Dead Sea" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: لا روسا · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
